corporation / partnership / disregarded>

Separate the **position** from the **evidence for it**. "We take this position" and "the return
taking it was accepted" are different facts; a register that merges them produces confidence where
a transcript check is what is actually required.

## Evidence status vocabulary

`TAKEN_AND_ACCEPTED` (return accepted; transcript checked) · `TAKEN_FILED_UNCONFIRMED` (return filed,
acceptance not yet verified) · `TAKEN_NOT_FILED` (decided, return not yet filed) · `PROPOSED`
(recommended, not decided) · `UNDETERMINED` (a prerequisite fact is unresolved)

This register lists current positions only. A superseded position's row is removed; the decision
memo that superseded it (`<scope-root>/decisions/`, see `supersession.md` §7) carries the history.
Rows cite a memo ID where one exists and never carry the reasoning.

Never write `IN EFFECT`, `RECORDED`, `POSITION READY`, or `FILED` for anything short of
`TAKEN_AND_ACCEPTED`.

